"""The query rewrite rule transforms `SELECT * FROM A INNER JOIN B ON condition1 WHERE condition2(A)` into `SELECT * FROM A INNER JOIN B ON condition1 AND condition2(A)` if `condition2` only involves columns from A. In this case, the conditions in the WHERE clause of the given SQL query can be logically applied to either input of the join to reduce the size of datasets before the join occurs.

The detailed changes of the given SQL query are:

- The conditions in the WHERE clause that do not reference columns from both tables involved in the join but can be logically applied to either input of the join to reduce the size of datasets before the join occurs are moved into the ON clause of the INNER JOIN or as a WHERE clause on a subquery of the respective side.

For example, the condition `ci.note = '(voice)'` is moved from the WHERE clause to the ON clause of the first INNER JOIN operation:

```sql
SELECT * 
FROM aka_name AS an,
     char_name AS chn,
     cast_info AS ci,
     company_name AS cn,
     info_type AS it,
     movie_companies AS mc,
     movie_info AS mi,
     name AS n,
     role_type AS rt,
     title AS t
WHERE ci.note = '(voice)'
  AND cn.country_code ='[us]'
  AND it.info = 'release dates'
  ...
INNER JOIN cast_info AS ci ON ci.note = '(voice)' 
...
```

Similarly, the conditions `mc.note LIKE '%(200%)%'` and `(mc.note LIKE '%(USA)%' OR mc.note LIKE '%(worldwide)%')` are moved from the WHERE clause to the ON clause of the second INNER JOIN operation:

```sql
SELECT * 
FROM aka_name AS an,
     char_name AS chn,
     cast_info AS ci,
     company_name AS cn,
     info_type AS it,
     movie_companies AS mc,
     movie_info AS mi,
     name AS n,
     role_type AS rt,
     title AS t
WHERE ...
INNER JOIN movie_companies AS mc ON mc.note LIKE '%(200%)%' AND (mc.note LIKE '%(USA)%' OR mc.note LIKE '%(worldwide)%') 
...
```

These transformations apply to the given SQL query because the conditions in the WHERE clause do not reference columns from both tables involved in the join but can be logically applied to either input of the join to reduce the size of datasets before the join occurs."""
